    <title>Planning with Long-Horizon Memory in
Tool-Using Agents</title>
    <summary>  We study how coding agents retain and reuse
context across long multi-step tool-use episodes, and show that an
explicit episodic memory outperforms naive context concatenation on
a suite of agentic planning benchmarks.
</summary>
